{"loc":"IBNATIYYA-FULL:v2p357#2","rows":[{"verses":["6:146"],"words":["*"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"After prohibitions for Muḥammad's community, Jewish prohibitions refute their claim God forbade nothing and Israel chose the restrictions; hādū and Jews were discussed in al-Baqara.","anchor":"لما ذكر الله عز وجل ما حرم على أمة محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم أعقب ذلك بذكر ما حرم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["6:146"],"words":["كُلَّ ذِى ظُفُرٍۢ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Dhi ẓufur includes camels, ostriches, geese, and similar animals with unsplit toes and nails. Abu Zayd restricts it to camels, which Ibn ʿAṭiyya rejects; Thaʿlab's predator/non-predator distinction fails because lions have nails.","anchor":"وكل ذي ظفر يراد به الإبل والنعام والإوز ونحوه من الحيوان","mentions":[]},{"verses":["6:146"],"words":["ظُفُرٍۢ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الجمهور والحسن والأعرج وأبو السمال قعنب","stance":"reports","claim":"The majority have ḍamma on both consonants; al-Ḥasan and al-Aʿraj have still fāʾ; Abu al-Sammāl Quʿnub has kasra on ẓāʾ and still fāʾ.","anchor":"وقرأ جمهور الناس «ظفر» بضم الظاء والفاء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["6:146"],"words":["شُحُومَهُمَآ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Forbidden fats include caul fat, kidney fat, and pure fat except what the verse exempts.","anchor":"وهي الثروب وشحم الكلى وما كان شحما خالصا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["6:146"],"words":["شُحُومَهُمَآ"],"type":"law","speaker":"ابن المنذر عن مالك وغيره","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn al-Mundhir reports in al-Ishrāf that Mālik and others prohibit fat from Jewish slaughter; this is the apparent Mudawwana ruling.","anchor":"فحكى ابن المنذر في الأشراف عن مالك وغيره منع أكل الشحم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["6:146"],"words":["شُحُومَهُمَآ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"On the view that ‘food of the People of Scripture’ in 5:5 means meat from their slaughter, what they cannot eat receives no valid slaughter and is like blood in Muslim slaughter; thus a Jew's camel or rabbit is not eaten.","anchor":"وطعام الذين أوتوا الكتاب حل لكم بأنه المطعوم من ذبائحهم","mentions":["5:5"]},{"verses":["6:146"],"words":["شُحُومَهُمَآ"],"type":"law","speaker":"مالك","stance":"reports","claim":"Another report says Mālik merely disliked fat from People of Scripture, not that he prohibited it; some permit such fat and their slaughter of animals forbidden to them when commissioned.","anchor":"وروي عن مالك رحمه الله كراهية الشحم من ذبائح أهل الكتاب دون تحريم","mentions":[]}]}
